The presence of multiple binding sites for S-adenosyl-L-methionine does not specifically distinguish PNMT from other enzymes that also utilize this cofactor. Therefore, while the binding of S-adenosyl-L-methionine is a real and relevant feature for the enzyme's function, it is not distinctive enough to be considered as the structural/functional basis for the GO term in this context.

